  "regions": [
    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "of a prince's eye-brows. कन्थाकञ्चुकिताः—कञ्चुकः एषां संजातः कञ्चु-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "किताः । कञ्चुक is a word of the तारकादि group and therefore it",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "takes the possessive aff. इत. Cf. ०स्यूतकंथाधरः. Sl. 96. Infra.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 67. दाक्षिणात्याः—Fr. दक्षिण + त्यक् meaning 'of that place';",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "poets of the Deccan who were masters of the Vaidarbhi style of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "composition which is regarded as the best. The Vaid. style",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "has ten qualities; see Kávyá. I. Sàh. Dar. describes it as माधुर्य-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "व्यञ्जकैर्वर्णै रचिता ललितात्मिका । अवृत्तिरल्पवृत्तिर्वा ( having no or very",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "few compounds ) वैदर्भीरीतिरिष्यते ॥ यद्यस्त्येवम्—but this is not",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "possible except in very few instances, and so the didactic chara-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "cter of the verse cannot be marred by its apparent acquiescence",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "in the enjoyment of pleasures.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 68. कल्पं स्थितं—Nouns showing duration of time are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "put in the Acc. case. Pán. II. 3. 5. For कल्प see notes, Nít. 16.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 69. मरणजन्मभयं हृदिस्थम्—If this fear is present in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "mind of man, he will try to obtain final beatitude; but if he is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "not aware of it, he will not work out his salvation. हृदिस्थम् an",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "aluk compound. Cf. this with the preceding sl.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 70. अजर—not subject to old age as it is निर्विकार; comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "सत्यं ज्ञानमनन्तं ब्रह्म' Tait. Up.; पुराणमजरं विदुः । Rag. X. 19. परमम्",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "—The highest. परा उत्कृष्टा मा शब्दन मायाख्या शक्तिर्यस्य । अथवा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "परा उत्कृष्टा मा शोभा यस्य तत्तथा । Râmarshi. विकासि—Cf The",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "S'rutis परास्य शक्तिर्विविधैव श्रूयते स्वाभाविकी ज्ञानबलक्रिया च and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "तमेव भान्तमनुभाति सर्वं तस्यैव भासा सर्वमिदं विभाति । विकल्प—विषय",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "Rámarshi; or rather fancies, dreams, as Mr. Telang takes it.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "अनुषङ्गिणः—those that follow, depend upon. कृपण०:—highly valued",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "by mean people. कृपण may also mean poor, to be pitied ( for los-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "ing sight of the real ); see com.; supra—०गहनाक्षेपकृपणः । Mis. 2.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r7",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 71. मानस Voc. sing.; some take मानसचापलेन as a comp.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "meaning 'with the swiftness of thought ( lit. mind ,' and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "suppose the verse to be addressed to man in general. Râmarshi",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "favours the former view. जातु—with the negative means",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "'Never.' आत्मनीनम्—आत्मने हितम् tending to one's benefit. आत्म-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "विश्वजनभोगोत्तरपदात् खः । Pân. V. 1. 9. आत्मन् , विश्वजन, and",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
